#edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1fbfa8ab-6879-57fc-b2d0-196f095281bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-112004" :question/problem "Given that $(x+3)$ is a factor of $f(x)={x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-9x-18,$ which of the following curves is generated by $y=f(x)?$\n\n(*Note: Figures not drawn to scale*)" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the function is a positive cubic curve because the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is positive.\n\nWe are told that $(x+3)$ is a factor of $f(x),$ so to find the other roots of $f(x)$ we use synthetic division to divide $f(x)$ by  $(x+3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2 & -9 & -18 \\\\  &  & -3 & 3 & 18 \\\\  & 1 & -1 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(x+3)({x}^{2}-x-6) \\\\  & =(x+3)(x+2)(x-3),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the roots of $f(x)$ are $x=-3,$ $x=-2,$ and $x=3.$ \n\nNow, let's find the $y$-intercept. To do that, we substitute $x=0,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(0+3)(0+2)(0-3) \\\\  & =(3)(2)(-3) \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we draw an inverted $\\text{S}$-shaped graph that passes through the three roots $x=-3,-2,3$ and has the $y$-intercept $y=-18,$ as follows:\n\n![](images/c3/c3d41c300747f4f0f18607351f2f03241c9a789ed70fe72e05c5a385b708c4c8.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570707 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115289 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "38c7027c-8dc4-5d3a-9a96-5d33d3b8c1c7" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Factored Cubic Curve with Negative Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84d8beff-2479-5088-bdac-e141e015a59c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/56/56f52c1e31d4e6224a222bdc57ee726848672332b7e1e6bed0c7d51db09a4f60.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570358} {:answer/id #uuid "a68e71cf-7bb8-52ab-aecd-7b06a8b6b148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7b/7b5f467f84f0c7d8b3c1dce432ae0c4db8117cde6730611ac4e48881a0bb4b69.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570419} {:answer/id #uuid "ad8813ef-4396-5a21-9fdd-ad55cb9aa352" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/13c3fb2aadb027fe3397b237e8c8027e1fcc7418106cc488e51f81062fa75e2e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570433} {:answer/id #uuid "d0a6cbb4-361d-51df-86ce-cc6151d8155e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/18/18a34470ca210b12544b90b520dfc4d2ed443231f55a2443ffbbdf31e72d61c1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570488} {:answer/id #uuid "d124ec48-3b27-5a60-951a-d15de5d7a40d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/47/472cf0dd7807c15e8e8334a163d1cfbfbbdcd974534e99b94222929048e72b31.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d124ec48-3b27-5a60-951a-d15de5d7a40d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/47/472cf0dd7807c15e8e8334a163d1cfbfbbdcd974534e99b94222929048e72b31.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570490} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9f032b0-b93a-57ee-ab00-0ed6113f8ef6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d85a230-c47c-5ffa-b563-dedfdd86c871" :question/math-academy-id "q-28074" :question/problem "Which of the following curves is generated by $y=-3(x+2)(x+1)(x-1)?$\n\n(*Note: Figures not drawn to scale*)" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the function is a product of $3$ linear binomials, so this function is a cubic function. Moreover, it is a negative cubic because if we were to expand the parentheses, the coefficient of the ${x}^{3}$ term would be negative:\n\n$$\n-3(x+2)(x+1)(x-1)=-3x\\cdot x\\cdot x+⋯=-3{x}^{3}+⋯\n$$\n\nThe equation is given in the factored form. So by the zero-product rule, we deduce that the roots are  $x=-2,$ $x=-1,$ and $x=1.$ \n\nWe now find the $y$-intercept of the curve by plugging the value $x=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3(0+2)(0+1)(0-1) \\\\  & =-3(2)(1)(-1) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we draw an $\\text{S}$-shaped graph that passes through the three roots $x=-2,-1,1$ and has the $y$-intercept $y=6,$ as follows:\n\n![](images/47/472cf0dd7807c15e8e8334a163d1cfbfbbdcd974534e99b94222929048e72b31.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570715 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e03f532e-bf46-5933-baf3-b59e42b7cc67" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing an Expanded Cubic Curve with Negative Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01480b4d-e433-5319-b7dd-b2b93fad7110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e3/e38995dc7545fe0b32a7214438397304b0fc2a3dd3b589f387ad7230b7740ee9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570121} {:answer/id #uuid "0ecb6cc8-9b1a-53ec-8594-8c498c333227" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/12/1222fb6503f602a7da1b84d73fa8ced3474ae7f65b695d9e71fba267712278b4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570148} {:answer/id #uuid "376e8047-36e1-5ce3-92f5-7608828fe9a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/21/21dec37151f40778b8f094d3ae68cd8716c993535e53496cf7f148817c72e345.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570220} {:answer/id #uuid "d264c026-fbc5-505c-b381-13549290748d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/84/8468568ef0a3848797191a51080e0a904f9a739f659286358341bb218012fb43.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570492} {:answer/id #uuid "f972b644-cb9f-5d42-8c7d-406b85ac2b37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/19/19a0cce27a712f55a6430100fe29d4ea1a323709f1a398fc2ce48c1b4fe3206b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "376e8047-36e1-5ce3-92f5-7608828fe9a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/21/21dec37151f40778b8f094d3ae68cd8716c993535e53496cf7f148817c72e345.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570220} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d149e3a-5f29-5983-a00c-27e7be6451ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570608}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c01baff-ab5f-57ff-be23-ce994353bbde" :question/math-academy-id "q-28365" :question/problem "Given that $x=2$ is a root of $f(x)=-{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-14x+8,$ which of the following curves is generated by $y=f(x)?$\n\n(*Note: Figures not drawn to scale*)" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice that the function is a negative cubic curve because the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is negative.\n\nWe are told that $x=2$ is a root of $f(x),$ which means that $(x-2)$ is a factor of $f(x).$ So, to find the other roots of $f(x)$ we use synthetic division to divide $f(x)$ by $(x-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 2 & -1 & 7 & -14 & 8 \\\\  &  & -2 & 10 & -8 \\\\  & -1 & 5 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(x-2)(-{x}^{2}+5x-4) \\\\  & =-(x-2)({x}^{2}-5x+4) \\\\  & =-(x-2)(x-1)(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the factors equal to zero, we find that the other roots of $f(x)$ are $x=1$ and $x=4.$ \n\nNow, let's find the $y$-intercept. To do that, we substitute $x=0,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-(0-2)(0-1)(0-4) \\\\  & =-(-2)(-1)(-4) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we draw an $S$-shaped graph that passes through the three roots $x=1,2,4$ and has the $y$-intercept $y=8,$ as follows:\n\n![](images/21/21dec37151f40778b8f094d3ae68cd8716c993535e53496cf7f148817c72e345.png)"}]}
